# Serve index.html for any path the host cannot find a file for, and let the
# Angular router decide from there.
#
# Without this, a visitor who opens /transactions directly — a bookmark, a
# shared link, or just pressing F5 — gets a 404: the host looks for a file at
# that path and there is none. Routing happens in the browser, after index.html
# has loaded.
#
# The 200 matters: it rewrites without redirecting, so the URL the user sees
# stays intact. Understood by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify alike.
/*    /index.html   200
